Force the IMPORT_EXECUTABLES cross-compile path under Emscripten.

MariaDB decides how to obtain its build-time codegen tools (comp_err,
gen_lex_hash, gen_lex_token, comp_sql, factorial, uca-dump) by checking
whether a crosscompiling emulator is available:

  CMakeLists.txt:431  IF(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND NOT DEFINED CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR)
  CMakeLists.txt:517  IF(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING OR DEFINED CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR)

Emscripten.cmake:376 unconditionally sets CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR to
node, so both guards resolve to "we can run target binaries" — MariaDB skips
IMPORT_EXECUTABLES and instead compiles the tools to wasm and runs them under
node during the build.

That does not work here. Those tools generate source files, i.e. they write
real files to the build tree, and Emscripten's default MEMFS is an in-memory
filesystem the build system cannot see. The tools would appear to succeed and
produce nothing.

Setting -DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR="" on the command line does not help:
Emscripten.cmake guards its assignment with NOT DEFINED, but MariaDB's checks
are also NOT DEFINED, so an empty-but-defined value still takes the wrong
branch in both places.

Hence an explicit opt-out: MARIADB_WASM_FORCE_IMPORT_EXECUTABLES.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -428,7 +428,7 @@
 ADD_SUBDIRECTORY(tpool)
 CHECK_SYSTEMD()

-IF(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND NOT DEFINED CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR)
+IF(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND (MARIADB_WASM_FORCE_IMPORT_EXECUTABLES OR NOT DEFINED CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR))
   SET(IMPORT_EXECUTABLES "IMPORTFILE-NOTFOUND" CACHE FILEPATH "Path to import_executables.cmake from a native build")
   INCLUDE(${IMPORT_EXECUTABLES})
 ENDIF()
@@ -514,7 +514,7 @@
 INCLUDE(for_clients)
 ADD_SUBDIRECTORY(scripts)
 ADD_SUBDIRECTORY(support-files)
 ADD_SUBDIRECTORY(extra/aws_sdk)

-IF(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING OR DEFINED CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR)
+IF(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING OR (DEFINED CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR AND NOT MARIADB_WASM_FORCE_IMPORT_EXECUTABLES))
   SET(EXPORTED comp_err comp_sql factorial uca-dump)
   IF(NOT WITHOUT_SERVER)
     SET(EXPORTED ${EXPORTED} gen_lex_hash gen_lex_token)
